<section class="value-case">
  <div class="container value-case-grid">
    <div class="value-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why hire Brighter Sites?</p>
      <h2>A website builder gives you tools. We give you a finished website—and someone responsible for it.</h2>
      <p class="value-lead">
        Platforms such as Wix can be a practical way to publish a website yourself. The difference is not whether the software can make a page. The difference is who is making the decisions, doing the technical work, checking the details, and improving the site after it launches.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you enjoy design, writing, SEO, analytics, mobile testing, domains, and ongoing maintenance, a DIY builder may fit you well. Brighter Sites is for practices that would rather spend that time on their clients and have a person who knows the website take responsibility for the web side of the practice.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="choice-grid" aria-label="DIY website builder compared with Brighter Sites">
      <article class="choice-card diy-card">
        <p class="choice-label">Using a DIY builder</p>
        <h3>You get the platform.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You choose and adapt the design.</li>
          <li>You decide how every page should be structured and written.</li>
          <li>You handle mobile, search, accessibility, analytics, and technical setup.</li>
          <li>You decide what the data means and what should change next.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="choice-card managed-card">
        <p class="choice-label">Working with Brighter Sites</p>
        <h3>You get the site and the expertise behind it.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A design and content structure built around your actual practice.</li>
          <li>Client pathways, mobile behavior, search structure, and launch details handled for you.</li>
          <li>A real person to contact who already understands how your site is built.</li>
          <li>Optional ongoing care that keeps the site from becoming a finished project nobody watches.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="video-capability">
  <div class="container video-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Video introductions & media</p>
      <h2>Let visitors hear from you before they ever schedule.</h2>
      <p>
        Brighter Sites can build responsive video sections for clinician introductions,
        practice welcomes, educational content, or other media. The Evergreen demo
        includes a live example of a YouTube video embedded directly into the site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="video-options">
      <article>
        <strong>YouTube Unlisted</strong>
        <p>
          An unlisted YouTube video can play on your website without appearing in
          normal YouTube search results or on your channel’s public video list.
          Anyone who obtains the direct video link can still watch or share it, so
          unlisted is less discoverable—not truly private.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <strong>Website-only playback</strong>
        <p>
          If you need tighter control, Brighter Sites can use a video host that
          supports domain-restricted embedding so playback can be limited to your
          approved website instead of relying on an ordinary public or unlisted link.
        </p>
      </article>

      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://evergreen.brightersites.app"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        See the embedded-video example on Evergreen →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="managed-growth">
  <div class="container growth-grid">
    <div class="growth-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Managed Growth</p>
      <h2>Analytics only matter if someone turns them into decisions.</h2>
      <p class="growth-lead">
        Connecting Google Analytics or Search Console is easy to call “analytics.” The useful part comes later: checking the data consistently, understanding what changed, deciding what is worth acting on, and then actually improving the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        With Managed Growth, Brighter Sites reviews the website each month, looks at analytics and conversion behavior, watches for SEO and content opportunities, and uses the included website-work time for practical updates. Each month also includes a written website report that explains the findings, trends, priorities, and recommended next improvements. The goal is not to hand you another dashboard to learn. It is to give you a clear picture of what matters and keep the site moving in the right direction.
      </p>

      <div class="growth-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/services/">See ongoing care plans</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Talk about your website →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="growth-board" aria-label="Example monthly website report">
      <div class="board-top">
        <span>MONTHLY WEBSITE REPORT</span>
        <strong>What changed, what matters, what comes next.</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Search visibility</h3>
          <p>Which pages and search queries are gaining or losing visibility?</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Visitor behavior</h3>
          <p>How are people arriving, what are they viewing, and which actions are they taking?</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Site health</h3>
          <p>Are there technical, performance, domain, or usability issues that need attention?</p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Recommendations</h3>
          <p>Which content, SEO, CTA, or site improvements should be prioritized next?</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="review-loop" aria-label="Monthly process">
        <span>Measure</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>Interpret</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>Prioritize</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>Improve</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="human-layer">
  <div class="container human-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">The human layer</p>
    <h2>Your website should not become another system you have to remember to manage.</h2>
    <p>
      A managed website means there is someone paying attention after launch. When your services change, a page underperforms, a search opportunity appears, or the site simply needs an update, you are not starting from scratch with a template editor or trying to remember how everything was configured months ago.
    </p>
    <p>
      You still make the business decisions. Brighter Sites handles the website work needed to carry those decisions through.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

